<title>NORWAY: WORK BEGINS ON NORWAY-GERMANY EUROPIPE II GASLINE.</title>
<headline>WORK BEGINS ON NORWAY-GERMANY EUROPIPE II GASLINE.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday work had begun on the 626 km (400 mile) Europipe II gas trunkline.</p>
<p>The pipe will run from the Kaarstoe terminal near Stavanger on the west coast of Norway to Dornum in northern Germany.</p>
<p>Work relating to the pipeline at the receiving station at Dornum will take place in August during a turnaround on the existing Europipe I line, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>Pipelaying is scheduled to begin in mid-1998 and to be completed by December.</p>
<p>Europipe II is due to come on stream in October, 1999 at a cost of 6.8 billion crowns ($876.8 million).</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
<p>($ = 7.755 Norwegian Crowns)</p>
